{"id":"0275c584-0ebe-4167-8fce-522be8730fa0","type":"level","createdDate":"2026-06-13T23:04:39.285Z","createdBy":"chaitanya.ponnapati@codeninjas.com","lastModifiedDate":"2026-06-13T23:04:39.285Z","lastModifiedBy":"chaitanya.ponnapati@codeninjas.com","attributes":{"tags":["CREATE"],"title":"Level 5","sequence":5,"activity":{"id":"4a4afabb-b733-4bc6-ae70-ae56756188c9","type":"activity","sequence":3,"group":{"id":"4a4afabb-b733-4bc6-ae70-ae56756188c9","type":"build","name":null,"sequence":8,"subgroups":[{"id":"4a4afabb-b733-4bc6-ae70-ae56756188c9","type":"subgroup","sequence":1,"name":"build 1","steps":[{"id":"bed6c188-af0a-4902-9691-5cd63ff96ea9","hints":"<p>❓Did you use the circle tool <img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/hba5ugwo.bhz.png\"> to draw a circle outline in black, positioned in the upper right part of the canvas, then fill it in with a light color, like this? </p>","senseiHelp":"<p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/lxkesmlp.2ww.png\"></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/r5z3t2p3.3ce.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Ask the ninja</strong>:</p><p>❓ Where might the circle image be placed on the canvas?</p><p>❓ What color might be used as the circle’s base color?</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Sensei Pro Tip</strong>:</p><p>💡 Point out to the ninja that the circle tool in the paint editor creates a circle from its center. That means that the ninja should position their mouse from wherever they want the center of the circle to appear.</p><p>💡 Make sure the ninja has positioned their circle in the upper right corner of the canvas, so that there is enough space for a shadow to be added to the bottom left of the canvas.</p>","instructions":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Begin the project by drawing a marble image!</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Click the </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Assets</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> menu along the top of the screen. Create a new image asset named </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">marble0</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Use the circle tool to draw a circle outlined in black. Position the circle in the upper right corner of the 16x16 canvas.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Then, use the fill tool to add a base color inside the outline. Consider using a light color for the marble, such as light blue (9).</span></p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"53e62f1a-660f-497e-8537-b4534b61713a","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓Did you use a light color to draw a </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">highlight</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">, and a dark color to draw a </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">cast shadow</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">, like this? </span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"></span><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/gd04xzz0.k0f.png\"></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/522za3st.0gi.png\"></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/eatqasth.o14.png\"></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Ask the ninja</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓ What is a </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">cast shadow</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">? Why should it be drawn </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">outside </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">of the marble’s outline?</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓ Why might tan be used as the </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">highlight</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> and dark purple be used as the </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">cast shadow</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">?</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Sensei Pro Tip</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">💡</span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Highlights </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">should be added in a color </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">lighter</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> than the base color. </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Shadows</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> should be added in a color </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">darker</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> than the base color.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">💡 Remind the ninja that the light source in this image is coming from the right, so the </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">highlight </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">should be placed on the upper right side of the marble and the </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">cast shadow </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">should be placed on the bottom left, outside of the marble’s outline.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">💡 Explain to the ninja that a </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">cast shadow</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> is a shadow that is cast by the object outside of the object itself. To demonstrate this, pixels should be added </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">outside</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> of the marble’s outline.</span></p>","instructions":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Add a </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">highlight</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> and a </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">cast shadow</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> to the marble image.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Duplicate the </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">marble0</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> asset, then rename the new asset </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">marble1</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">The light source in this image will be coming from the upper right corner of the canvas, and will shine across the marble, creating a </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">highlight </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">on the upper right part of the marble and a </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">cast shadow</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> on the lower left side.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Select the tan color (13) to draw a few pixels to create a </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">highlight</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> on the upper right corner of the marble image.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Select the dark purple color (12) to draw a </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">cast shadow</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> on the lower left side of the marble, outside of the outline. </span></p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"29f858c8-1dab-48f4-b330-38c845173904","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓Did you create a </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">form shadow</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> and a </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">terminator</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> along the lower left part of the marble, like this?</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"></span><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/2tmyyrfg.lfj.png\"></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/uzihikd1.0jt.png\"></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/pfhqigau.rzf.png\"></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Ask the ninja</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓ What is a </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">form shadow </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">and a </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">terminator</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">? What do they add to the marble image?</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓ What colors might be used to draw the </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">form shadow </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">and </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">terminator</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> on the marble image?</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Sensei Pro Tip</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">💡 A </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">form shadow</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> is the part of the object not hit directly by light. The </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">terminator </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">is the line between where the light hits and where the </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">shadow </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">is created.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">💡 Point out to the ninja that a color that is darker than the marble base color should be used to draw the </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">form shadow</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> and a medium color between the marble base color and the </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">shadow</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> color should be used to draw the </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">terminator</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">.</span></p>","instructions":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Add shading to the body of the marble image.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Duplicate the </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">marble1</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> asset, then rename the new asset </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">marble2</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Draw a </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">form shadow</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> on the lower left side of the marble to show where the light would not hit the marble directly. Use a color that is darker than the marble color, such as blue (8).</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Then, add a few pixels to the </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">form shadow</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> to create the </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">terminator</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">, which is the transition between the </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">shadow</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> and the light area on the object. Use a medium color between the marble color and the </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">shadow</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> color, such as teal (6).</span></p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"947689c0-5621-414f-abd7-f9732e23e2dd","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓Did you create a </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">reflection highlight</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> as part of the </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">highlight</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> in the right corner, then add </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">bounce light</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> into the </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">form shadow</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">, like this?</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"></span><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/jliqxgnn.xux.png\"></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/uvmq5z5k.yix.png\"></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/h15bkbs0.uv3.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Ask the ninja</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓ What is a </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">reflection highlight </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">and </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">bounce light</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">? What do they add to the marble image?</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓ What color might be used to draw the </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">reflection highlight </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">and </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">bounce light </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">on the marble image?</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Sensei Pro Tip</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">💡 The </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">reflection highlight</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> represents the brightest spot on the object. Because the light source in this image is coming from the right, the </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">reflection highlight </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">should also be placed on the upper right side of the image.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">💡 The </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">bounce light </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">represents the light that is bouncing off the ground back onto the object. This should be drawn on the lower left corner of the image, inside the outline.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">💡 Point out to the ninja that a very bright color should be used to draw the </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">reflection highlight</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> and a color that is brighter than the </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">cast shadow</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> should be used to draw the </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">bounce light</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">.</span></p>","instructions":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Add the finishing touches to the marble’s shading.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Duplicate the </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">marble2</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> asset, then rename the new asset </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">marble3</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Inside the </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">highlight</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> in the right corner of the marble, add a few pixels to represent the </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">reflection highlight</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">, which is the brightest spot on the object. Use a very bright color for this, such as white (1).</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Then, use another color, such as purple (10) to add some </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">bounce light</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> to the </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">form shadow </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">to create the effect that light is bouncing off the ground back onto the object.</span></p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"21a69e31-30b0-4d66-8e5d-16d9e6fe41a3","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓Did you smooth out the edges of the marble to look more rounded, like this? </span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"></span><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/h23m5q3b.qcj.png\"></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/dpayybuu.wb2.png\"></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/yp2dr0n2.iny.png\"></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Ask the ninja</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓ Where might pixels be placed to make the edges of the marble appear less “pointy”?</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓ What color might be used to smooth the edges of the marble image?</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Sensei Pro Tip</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">💡 Encourage the ninja to tinker with placing pixels around the edges of the marble image to soften its image. Remind them that they can zoom in and out of the image to see how the placement of the pixels look at a smaller scale.</span></p>","instructions":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Smooth out the shape of the marble so it looks more rounded.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Duplicate the </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">marble3</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> asset, then rename the new asset </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">marble4</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Smooth out the edges of the marble to make them look less “pointy”. Replace pixels in the outline, or add pixels around the curved edges of the marble, using a neutral color like light purple (11) to make the marble appear more rounded on screen.</span></p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"73f3bb09-84a6-4a45-8470-5e4fbad0e872","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓Did you type </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">assets</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">, a dot operator, the asset type and the asset name</span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> </strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">inside 2 backticks </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">``</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> for each element in the </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">marbleImages</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> array?</span></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/d0yeceaq.izs.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Ask the ninja</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓ Did you place the marble image assets in the correct order in the </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">marbleImages</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> array?</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓ What background color might be used to display the marble images on screen?</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Sensei Pro Tip</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">💡 Make sure the number of each image asset matches the corresponding index in the array so that each image adds onto the previous one.</span></p>","instructions":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Set the scene to display the marble images on screen!</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Return to the JavaScript editor, then add a </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">// project initialization</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> comment at the top. Below, declare a </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">marbleImages</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> array that stores the 5 marble image assets.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Then, add a </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">// project start</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> comment and set a background color underneath.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Click ▶</span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><em> </em></strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">to see the chosen background color appear on screen.</span></p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"9ac67b09-69e7-49a4-94ef-319ec69c16b0","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓Did you add an xOffset value (</span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">25</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">) with a spacing value (</span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">25</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">), multiplied by the counter variable </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">i</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> like this: </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">(25 + (25 * i))</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">, to set each sprite’s x-position?</span></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/1z33olrb.u5o.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Ask the ninja</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓ What values might you use to offset the sprites from the left side of the screen and to space out each sprite?</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓ How do the marble images appear on screen?</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Sensei Pro Tip</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">💡 Encourage the ninja to test out their code to make sure the sprites are placed correctly on screen. Prompt them to consider which values should be added together and which should be multiplied to correctly position the images.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">💡 Point out to the ninja that they made small updates to the marble image in each iteration. Have them compare the first and last images to see how the drawing progressed over time.</span></p>","instructions":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Display the marble image from each step of the drawing process on screen!</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Under </span><span style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">// project start</span><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">, use a </span><span style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">for</span><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> loop to create 5 sprites. Use the loop’s counter variable to select a different image from the </span><span style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">marbleImages</span><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> array, each time the loop runs.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Set the x-position of the sprites by adding a value to offset the left side of the screen with the spacing between each sprite, multiplied by the loop’s counter variable. Set the y-position to a coordinate in the middle of the screen.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Click ▶</span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><em> </em></strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">to see each marble image displayed on screen!</span></p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"786bfb04-1971-431c-9ebb-01972252baf0","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓Did you update all 4 parameters in the </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">runImageAnimation</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> function so that the images in the </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">marbleImages</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> array continuously loop ?</span></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/bxggtigf.boc.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Ask the ninja</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓ Why might the </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">runImageAnimation</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> function be useful for showing multiple iterations of an image?</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓ What might the frameInterval and loop parameters be set to so that the images continuously rotate at a reasonable rate?</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Sensei Pro Tip</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">💡 The </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">runImageAnimation</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> function can be useful for showing how an image changes over time. In this context, because the marble image was slowly added onto, the image animation helps the user visualize how it transformed in each version.</span></p>","instructions":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Add image animation to show the progression across the marble images!</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Under </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">// project start</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">, create a new sprite with its image set to the first element of the </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">marbleImages</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> array. Position the sprite to appear </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">above</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> the 5 sprites created in the </span><span style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">for</span><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> loop.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Animate the sprite’s image to rotate through each of the elements in the </span><span style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">marbleImages</span><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> array. Update the frameInterval and loop parameters so that the images continuously cycle through.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Click ▶</span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><em> </em></strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">to see the development of the custom marble image on screen!</span></p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null}],"title":"Pixel Art Shading - Shadows & Reflections","project":{"editor":{"filters":[{"na